<!-- Field map of the item entity: which attribute of the client's item table corresponds to which attribute of
     the server's item file. It names files, elements and attributes only; it holds no row of either side.

     How it was made: the same ids were read on both sides of one shipped data set and every pair of fields was
     compared id by id. Only ids with exactly one row and one <environment> on each side were compared ("sample").
       compared      ids where both sides carry the field
       agree/differ  of those, how many correspond under "convert"
       clientAbsent  ids where only the server carries it; "default" is given when the server holds that one
                     value in 97% or more of them (an absent client attribute then counts as that value)
       loader        yes = the attribute name was also found in the client's item loader
       confidence    high: 97% or more agree and at least 20 compared; medium: 90% or more; low: the rest
     Fields are written as element-path@attribute, the path counted from <environment>.

     map         both sides are kept equal: a mod that changes one side changes the other (see README)
     candidate   a pair with different names that agrees too rarely to be trusted; reported, never synced
     clientOnly  no counterpart in the server file
     serverOnly  no counterpart in the client table

     convert     same     equal text
                 bool     client true/false, server 1/0
                 numlist  numbers separated by commas, compared as numbers (the server writes 0.000000, 0.000000)
                 affix    the client may hold the bare name, the server holds prefix + name + suffix
                 pick     the server holds a list; the client holds the same list, or the one element chosen by
                          the "index" field of the server file (counted from 1) -->
